        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Ongoing abdominal distension, described as 'like a balloon'; mild shortness of breath when lying flat; oliguria, urinating 2–3 times a day with only a dribble; mild nausea, decreased appetite, and weakness. Denies fever, rigors, vomiting, haematemesis, melaena, and confusion today; denies chest pain, new peripheral oedema (reports baseline mild ankle swelling), frank haematuria, and dysuria."
      }
